{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/855694-how-does-frenzy-work-in-w20","id":855694,"title":"How does Frenzy work in W20?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-30T07:48:03-07:00","id":855694,"title":"How does Frenzy work in W20?","content":"Hello, here it come other questions from a rooky Werewolf ST.<br /> <br /> 1) Reading on page 261-262 it says any Rage roll with 4+ successes sends into Frenzy. Will it be a Berserk or Fox Frenzy?<br /> I guess the answer is the ST decides based on the stimulus, BUT: it doesn\u2019t make much sense to me a character a character with Rage 10 has more changes to Fly then a character with Rage 1 when facing a scary situation.<br /> <br /> On page 436, the victim of Roar of the Wyrm resists the Fox Frenzy with a Will Power roll (WP makes more sense for a Fox Frenzy roll to me than Rage).<br /> It would also make sense to me a character gets into Fox Frenzy when fails or a Rage roll, in a fashion of Fight or Fly reaction.<br /> <br /> Question 1a) Does a character get into Fox Frenzy when he gets 4+ success on a Rege roll while facing a scary situation?<br /> Question 1b) If the answer to 1a is &quot;yes&quot; is it a non-sense in the rules or I don't understand what Rage is in this game? If the latest, please, explain to me.<br /> <br /> 2) When the character gets the roll to get into Frenzy can spend a single WP point to prevent the Frenzy to happen, but if he lets the Frenzy start using WP only allows the character to choose the targets. Is this correct?<br /> <br /> 3) Half of my PCs have higher Rage than Gnosis, this means they'll attack their pack mates while in Frenzy. Is there any mechanic in the game allowing the character to end the Frenzy or it will only end when he kills all the other PCs or the other PCs kill/KO him?<br /> In Vampire, the character has to get 5 successes in a Self-Control extended roll.<br /> <br /> 4) In Full Moon the Frenzy difficulty for an Ahroun is 3. Moots are always run during Full Moon. Does this means moots always end with a significant number of dead Garous?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11010-ersito","name":"erSito","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T08:05:00-07:00","id":855703,"title":"","content":"3) I've always ruled that being a pack with a totem negates this<br /> <br /> 4) read about how a moot is run, there are plenty of opportunities for werewolves off all auspices to burn off excessive &quot;energy&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T08:43:00-07:00","id":855715,"title":"","content":"1) I'm told that Dark Ages Werewolf had some more concrete examples of which one would apply.<br /> <br /> 2) Yes, it's cheaper to just choke it down in the beginning.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/855694-how-does-frenzy-work-in-w20?p=855703#post855703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) I've always ruled that being a pack with a totem negates this<br /> <br /> 4) read about how a moot is run, there are plenty of opportunities for werewolves off all auspices to burn off excessive &quot;energy&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't matter, though, because Ahroun are at least skirting the line for frenzy at a minimum; 0.7 (likelihood of success per die) x 5 (minimum Ahroun Rage) = 3.5. And if you're in Crinos, the difficulty is 1 lower. There are, meanwhile, no rolls for being &quot;exhausted&quot; making frenzy more difficult, unless you get into That Damned Rite from CoG Revised, and even it didn't actually give any mechanical details on how it was supposed to work with the dice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T09:17:31-07:00","id":855733,"title":"","content":"A few other things:<br /> <br /> Remember that Rank increases Frenzy difficulties The game generally expects you not to get to large levels of Rage until you start Ranking up, which helps most of the established Garou keep themselves in check. Higher Ranking Garou are generally going to be more capable of stopping a Cliath or Fostern that's losing it.<br /> <br /> There's also a Gifts/Fetishes/etc. that can be used to tamp down on things if tensions are high and lots of high Rage characters are around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T09:38:28-07:00","id":855747,"title":"","content":"In my games, It's been a thing that once the fight is over, the pack tends to piledrive the frenzying ahroun and whack him with bashing damage till he finally drops. They even developed special pak tactics for incapacitating their own. The Ahroun actually helped them develop the tactic after he caused a battle scar to the Galilard. Mind you, the frenzying maniacs tended to toss themselves out of the fight fast enough once the frenzy started, so that was less of a problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T04:42:03-08:00","id":1020280,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> Coming back to this topic to ask a new question. How does a berserk Frenzy ends? Is there any mechanic to get out of it (like getting 5 success on a self-control extended roll) or the Garou stays in Frenzy the entire scene?<br /> <br /> Thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11010-ersito","name":"erSito","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T06:41:02-08:00","id":1020353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OPP, on pg. 261 of W20,</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A werewolf can only come out of frenzy once the triggering situation is over. Once he\u2019s escaped, the player rolls Willpower (difficulty equaling the Garou\u2019s own Rage) to escape the frenzy. If the roll fails, the player can try again next turn with no increase in difficulty.</div> </div> </div> </div>So the answer to #3 is &quot;It depends on what triggered the Frenzy in the first place.&quot; If your Packmate triggered your Frenzy, it will continue at least until your Packmate is no longer a valid target, whether through their death, your death, or them being removed from your presence. If a Wyrm-thing triggered your Frenzy, your Packmates are perfectly safe unless they present themselves as a target such as by getting in your way or standing next to you when the Wyrm-thing goes down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T07:13:31-08:00","id":1020380,"title":"","content":"W20 makes it so you can roll to come out of a frenzy every round... game designers must have decided to give us a break... after all even a momentary outburst in crinos, or hispo, has probaly breached the veil if in public...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T13:30:48-08:00","id":1020605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/855694-how-does-frenzy-work-in-w20?p=1020353#post1020353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So the answer to #3 is &quot;It depends on what triggered the Frenzy in the first place.&quot; If your Packmate triggered your Frenzy, it will continue at least until your Packmate is no longer a valid target, whether through their death, your death, or them being removed from your presence. If a Wyrm-thing triggered your Frenzy, your Packmates are perfectly safe unless they present themselves as a target such as by getting in your way or standing next to you when the Wyrm-thing goes down.</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming a Wyrm creature triggered the Frenzy and is now dead or gone, and the packmate has failed the roll to come out of the Frenzy, there is a chance he/she will attack packmates (if their Rage/Gnosis ratio is off) by RAW.<br /> <br /> I agree with the statements above in general, but the &quot;perfectly safe&quot; bit isn't 100% correct imo. Depending on rolls, there could be a round or 3 where the character is still lashing out at anything/everyone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T16:05:26-08:00","id":1020692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/855694-how-does-frenzy-work-in-w20?p=1020605#post1020605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assuming a Wyrm creature triggered the Frenzy and is now dead or gone, and the packmate has failed the roll to come out of the Frenzy, there is a chance he/she will attack packmates (if their Rage/Gnosis ratio is off) by RAW.<br /> <br /> I agree with the statements above in general, but the &quot;perfectly safe&quot; bit isn't 100% correct imo. Depending on rolls, there could be a round or 3 where the character is still lashing out at anything/everyone.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>If a Wyrm-thing triggered your Frenzy, your Packmates are perfectly safe unless they present themselves as a target such as by getting in your way <b>or standing next to you when the Wyrm-thing goes down.</b></i></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Bolded for emphasis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T17:08:19-08:00","id":1020717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/855694-how-does-frenzy-work-in-w20?p=1020692#post1020692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bolded for emphasis.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. Been a long week. Wasn't trying to say you were wrong by any means anyways. I was trying to clarify circumstances when it could be an issue.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T18:37:29-08:00","id":1020745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/855694-how-does-frenzy-work-in-w20?p=1020717#post1020717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair enough. Been a long week. Wasn't trying to say you were wrong by any means anyways. I was trying to clarify circumstances when it could be an issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>It has most definitely been one of those. I fell asleep at my desk at work this afternoon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T00:13:12-08:00","id":1020791,"title":"","content":"Thank you very much. A single success in the WP roll is enough to get out of the Frenzy? Not accumulating 5 like in vampire?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11010-ersito","name":"erSito","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T05:28:04-08:00","id":1020830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>erSito</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/855694-how-does-frenzy-work-in-w20?p=1020791#post1020791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you very much. A single success in the WP roll is enough to get out of the Frenzy? Not accumulating 5 like in vampire?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. Once the triggering event is over. Otherwise, the Garou is spending Willpower instead of rolling it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T09:46:21-08:00","id":1020926,"title":"","content":"There have to be differences between be constantly fighting against your inner fury, and actually use it as a weapon. Werewolves and Vampires have arguably similar conditions on this, but almost completely distinct takes on the matter.<br /> <br /> A Garou that was constantly fighting the Rage, and never using it, could arguably use rules similar to Vampires, but that probably would mean one of those poor bastards that went crazy with the condition without any other Garou to help understanding. It wouldn't be as easy the other way around, since Vampires don't have the means to capitalize on the Frenzy and inner fury the way the Garou do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T09:54:25-08:00","id":1020930,"title":"","content":"I would also add that the Beast in Vampire is treated as kind of an alien entity of base desires. It is something to be resisted and fought. Rage in Werewolf is a natural part of the Garou. It isn't something they battle <i>against</i> (this is admittedly arguable).<br /> <br /> Even from a mechanics standpoint this proves true. Vampires roll to resist Frenzy, while Werewolves roll to see if their Rage overtakes them. The rolls are approached from opposite sides.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T09:59:22-08:00","id":1020933,"title":"","content":"Its a matter of relation. They can even be the same thing in setting, since they were never fully explained, nor will, and both theoretically came from the Wyrm. But for a Garou, it is both natural to its constitution and a tool its body can rely on. For vampires, though, it is just alien, since their original make-up is that of a normal human, and the Curse don't rely in any way in fury for power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T10:33:05-08:00","id":1020940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/855694-how-does-frenzy-work-in-w20?p=1020930#post1020930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would also add that the Beast in Vampire is treated as kind of an alien entity of base desires. It is something to be resisted and fought. Rage in Werewolf is a natural part of the Garou. It isn't something they battle <i>against</i> (this is admittedly arguable).<br /> <br /> Even from a mechanics standpoint this proves true. Vampires roll to resist Frenzy, while Werewolves roll to see if their Rage overtakes them. The rolls are approached from opposite sides.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Rage powers Garou though the horrors of fighting the Wyrm. A normal person or Kinfolk would crumble in the face of a bane. A Garou would just get pissed. However, like any weapon, Rage is dangerous. A Garou needs to learn control to make best use of rage. And to make sure no innocents fall victim to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T11:00:33-08:00","id":1020952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/855694-how-does-frenzy-work-in-w20?p=1020940#post1020940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Rage powers Garou though the horrors of fighting the Wyrm. A normal person or Kinfolk would crumble in the face of a bane. A Garou would just get pissed. However, like any weapon, Rage is dangerous. A Garou needs to learn control to make best use of rage. And to make sure no innocents fall victim to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't necessarily agree with these statements. Mechanically, Rage does no such thing. Assuming you aren't a Fera that only Berserk Frenzies (Gurahl, Rokea I think, and Get with a Gift...off the top of my head), Rage also makes you Fox Frenzy. So yes, it greatly helps Garou fight the Wyrm, but it isn't (generally) a defensive stat you use to fight fear.<br /> <br /> Also, Kinfolk or normal people don't collapse in horror at the sight of a Bane (assuming said Bane doesn't induce Delirium somehow). They <i>could</i> obviously, but there isn't some innate need to. If you've seen the show Stranger Things, I feel that covered a variety of human reactions to seeing a Bane. Honestly, the entire show reminded me a lot of the WoD. It could easily be a story of (mostly) humans dealing with a thinned/ripped Gauntlet and a local Bane.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T11:10:06-08:00","id":1020954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/855694-how-does-frenzy-work-in-w20?p=1020952#post1020952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't necessarily agree with these statements. Mechanically, Rage does no such thing. Assuming you aren't a Fera that only Berserk Frenzies (Gurahl, Rokea I think, and Get with a Gift...off the top of my head), Rage also makes you Fox Frenzy. So yes, it greatly helps Garou fight the Wyrm, but it isn't (generally) a defensive stat you use to fight fear.<br /> <br /> Also, Kinfolk or normal people don't collapse in horror at the sight of a Bane (assuming said Bane doesn't induce Delirium somehow). They <i>could</i> obviously, but there isn't some innate need to. If you've seen the show Stranger Things, I feel that covered a variety of human reactions to seeing a Bane. Honestly, the entire show reminded me a lot of the WoD. It could easily be a story of (mostly) humans dealing with a thinned/ripped Gauntlet and a local Bane.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's been a while since I played Werewolf and to be honest, I don't know much about the Fera. I guess I need to read the section on Rage again. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T11:17:01-08:00","id":1020955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/855694-how-does-frenzy-work-in-w20?p=1020954#post1020954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It's been a while since I played Werewolf and to be honest, I don't know much about the Fera. I guess I need to read the section on Rage again. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't been gotten to play in longer than I would like. It was one of my favorite WoD games though, along with VtDA. A lot of what I talk about on here (the Forums) is from memory, so I'm sometimes wrong (it happens). I have the 20th Anniversary books and reference them when needed, but if there are changes in 20th that don't stand out, I am probably referencing Revised. I don't think they changed much about Rage though between the editions.<br /> <br /> Rage covering both Berserk and Fox Frenzies can sometimes be confusing, since most of the fluff and artwork depict Berserk Frenzies.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T11:23:02-08:00","id":1020957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/855694-how-does-frenzy-work-in-w20?p=1020955#post1020955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't been gotten to play in longer than I would like. It was one of my favorite WoD games though, along with VtDA. A lot of what I talk about on here (the Forums) is from memory, so I'm sometimes wrong (it happens). I have the 20th Anniversary books and reference them when needed, but if there are changes in 20th that don't stand out, I am probably referencing Revised. I don't think they changed much about Rage though between the editions.<br /> <br /> Rage covering both Berserk and Fox Frenzies can sometimes be confusing, since most of the fluff and artwork depict Berserk Frenzies.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I am trying to pin down rage from a RP perspective. Is it just the flight/fight response kicked up to eleven?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T12:16:50-08:00","id":1020967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/855694-how-does-frenzy-work-in-w20?p=1020957#post1020957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I am trying to pin down rage from a RP perspective. Is it just the flight/fight response kicked up to eleven?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not exactly, but also yes. Helpful I know (sorry). I think starting with that perspective though is a lot closer than just looking at it as super-anger (which it <i>also</i> is).<br /> <br /> I began a longer post, but will come back to it later when I have more time.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T13:34:37-08:00","id":1020990,"title":"","content":"You can think of Rage better in terms of Primal Urge (than the actual Primal Urge ability, by the way). It is the internal beast, the most instinctual emotions, up to eleven.<br /> <br /> As strange as it looks, it is easier to understand Rage reading about Vampire's Beast. Isn't the same, but is close enough and better explained.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T13:51:54-08:00","id":1020995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>erSito</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/855694-how-does-frenzy-work-in-w20#post855694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question 1a) Does a character get into Fox Frenzy when he gets 4+ success on a Rege roll while facing a scary situation?<br /> Question 1b) If the answer to 1a is &quot;yes&quot; is it a non-sense in the rules or I don't understand what Rage is in this game? If the latest, please, explain to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the Fight or Flight response. I generally let the player decide if they want to go into Fox Frenzy or not as it should be based on what level of threat they perceive it to be. PCs on the whole do not like it whenever the ST jumps in to control their character. I just make it known to them that is if they chose Bezerk Frenzy and the fight turns against them, there isn't a whole lot they can do.<br /> <br /> You have an interesting question on why is it Rage if the result is to flee from something. Usually intense anger doesn't cause people to run away from what angers them. That's because Rage isn't &quot;intense anger&quot;. It is a supernatural force. It is an incarnation of the &quot;Beast&quot; which is purposefully vague, but which I consider to be the primal animalistic instinct for survival. That instinct for survival can translate into destroying whatever it is that threatens you. But it is an equally valid response to run away from something that is a threat you can't handle.<br /> <br /> A soldier in combat who cracks under the strain of combat and considers even civilians a threat that he shoots with his gun in under Berzerk Frenzy.<br /> <br /> A civilian in a crowded building that is on fire which pushes and stampedes and tramples people in order to get to the exit door (and who may even create the conditions that prevent anyone from getting out, such as pushing against someone who needs to PULL open the door to escape, but can't because of the mass of people pushing against him and therefore the very door he's trying to open) is in Fox Frenzy.<br /> <br /> In both cases, the mind is shut down and instincts take over. That is what the Rage Roll for Frenzy represents. It is not quite equivalent for Garou because humans don't actually have Rage (just as they don't have the Beast like vampires and Garou do). But that same part of the brain is where that supernatural force of the Garou &quot;resides&quot;. Because of that, it is even more strong than in a normal human.<br /> <br /> Normally in non-Frenzy situations, the Garou is able to consciously and mystically tap into that power to perform various supernatural acts. In a Frenzy situation, it is pure instinct taking over as opposed to a conscious attempt to use the force for an effect.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T15:35:19-08:00","id":1021045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/855694-how-does-frenzy-work-in-w20?p=1020995#post1020995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...stuff...</div> </div> </div> </div>Very well said.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}